         <p>Everything you ever wanted to know about cats.</p>
     </header>

     <main>
         <section class="faq-container">
             <div class="example">
                 <h2>
                     <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq1-content" class="faq-trigger" id="faq1-trigger">
                         Why do cats purr?
                     </button>
                 </h2>
                 <div class="details" id="faq1-content" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq1-trigger">
                     <p>Cats purr for many reasons. While often a sign of contentment, they also purr to self-soothe when stressed or in pain. The frequency of a cat's purr (between 25 and 150 Hertz) has even been shown to improve bone density and promote healing!</p>
                 </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
                 <h2>
                     <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq2-content" class="faq-trigger" id="faq2-trigger">
                         Why do cats have whiskers?
                     </button>
                 </h2>
                 <div class="details" id="faq2-content" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq2-trigger">
                     <p>Whiskers are highly sensitive tactile hairs that act as a sensory guide. They help cats navigate in the dark, judge the width of openings, and detect changes in air currents, which is useful for hunting prey.</p>
                 </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
                 <h2>
                     <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq3-content" class="faq-trigger" id="faq3-trigger">
                         Why do cats love boxes?
                     </button>
                 </h2>
                 <div class="details" id="faq3-content" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq3-trigger">
                     <p>Boxes provide a sense of security and safety. As ambush predators, cats love to hide in confined spaces where they can observe their surroundings without being seen. They also help keep them warm by providing insulation!</p>
                 </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
                 <h2>
                     <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq4-content" class="faq-trigger" id="faq4-trigger">
                         How much sleep do cats need?
                     </button>
                 </h2>
                 <div class="details" id="faq4-content" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq4-trigger">
                     <p>On average, cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Some can even sleep up to 20 hours! This is an evolutionary trait from their wild ancestors who needed to conserve energy for short, intense bursts of hunting activity.</p>
                 </div>
             </div>
         </section>
     </main>

     <footer>
         <p>&copy; 2024 Feline Facts Inc.</p>
     </footer>

     <script>
         document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
             const triggers = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-trigger');

             triggers.forEach(trigger => {
                 const panel = document.getElementById(trigger.getAttribute('aria-controls'));

                 // Initialize state: collapsed by default.
                 // We do this in JS to ensure content is visible if JS fails.
                 trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                 panel.hidden = true;

                 trigger.addEventListener('click', () => {
                     const isExpanded = trigger.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';

                     // Toggle state
                     trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !isExpanded);
                     panel.hidden = isExpanded;
                 });
             });
         });
     </script>
